{{also|ablaté}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|ablatum|lang=la}} past participle of {{term|auferre||to remove|lang=la}}; {{term|au-||away|lang=la}} + {{term|ferre||to carry|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{a|US}} {{IPA|/æ.ˈbleɪt/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|ablat|ing}}

# {{transitive}} To [[remove]] or [[decrease]] something by [[cutting]], [[erosion]], [[melting]], [[evaporation]], or [[vaporization]].
# {{intransitive}} To [[undergo]] ablation.

====Derived terms====
* [[ablator]]

====Related terms====
* [[ablation]]
* [[ablative]]

